---
description: One file per resource or model; helper then util only after 1000 code lines
alwaysApply: true
---

# File colocation

Backend domain code lives in four modules: `access`, `masters`, `knowledge`,
`conversation`. One production file per resource (service + repository + named
`*Http` adapters, or worker handler + its persistence). One production file per
model in `backend/src/models/`.

**API URL map:** all registration (method, path, access helpers, handler) lives
in `backend/src/http/route.js`. Paths are `/{module}/{file}/{action}/:ids…`.
Handler names are product verbs (`createUserHttp`, not `postUsersHttp`). See
`http-routes.mdc` — do not add per-resource `*Routes` plugins.

Do not add a helper or util up front. Do not add a file per function. Do not add
a `helpers/` folder or a shared util dumped across resources. Do not add a file
that nothing in production calls (including unused feature barrels and unused UI
kits). Do not re-export a symbol from a module `index.js` that no other file
imports from that barrel.

## Overflow (code lines only)

The **1000 code-line cap applies to production files under `src/` only**.
Files under `backend/tests/` and `frontend/tests/` are exempt.

A production file must not exceed **1000 code lines**. Do not count blank
lines, `//` comments, or `/* */` / JSDoc blocks.

- If `resource.js` would exceed 1000 code lines, add **one** `resource.helper.js`
  used only by that file. Public functions stay on `resource.js`.
- If `resource.helper.js` would exceed 1000 code lines, add **one**
  `resource.util.js` used only by that helper.
- Do not add a second helper.

```js
// BAD — one unused helper, own file
// organizationScope.js
export function assertOrganizationPathMatchesPrincipal(pathOrgId, principal) {
  if (String(pathOrgId) !== String(principal.orgId)) {
    throw ApiError.fromCode('NOT_FOUND');
  }
}

// GOOD — live in the resource file that owns the concern
export function createAuthorizePreHandler(requiredPermissions) {
  return async function authorize(request) {
    if (String(request.params.orgId) !== String(request.principal.orgId)) {
      throw ApiError.fromCode('NOT_FOUND');
    }
  };
}
```
